nd: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n\nHepatic Vascular Disorders vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst:\n  Favours first:  abducens palsy, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abnormal ovarian morphology, calcified ovarian cyst, changes in bowel movements, dizziness\n\nEctopic Pregnancy vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abnormal ovarian morphology, calcified ovarian cyst, changes in bowel movements, dizziness\n\nRelated to Biliary Tract Obstruction: bile duct disease, bile reflux, biliary tract neoplasm (disease)\n\nRelated to Hepatic Vascular Disorders: budd-chiari syndrome, hepatic infarction, hepatic vein thrombosis\n\nRelated to Ectopic Pregnancy: abdominal ectopic pregnancy, female reproductive system disease, ovarian ectopic pregnancy\n\nRelated to Ruptured Ovarian Cyst: corpus luteum cyst, malignant ovarian cyst, neonatal ovarian cyst\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → arthralgia → Biliary Tract Obstruction\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → abdominal distention → Biliary Tract Obstruction\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → shoulder pain → Hepatic Vascular Disorders"}
